                <pb facs="1204" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1054"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4960/54.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Refers to Embassy’s No. 42 of May 3, and informs him that he is authorized to
                    give the adhesion of this Government to customs increase.)</p>
            </div>
